<item><title>Congo faces Guinea in March for spot at U23 Africa Cup of Nations finals</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-faces-guinea-in-march-for-spot-at-u23-africa-cup-of-49e741/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-faces-guinea-in-march-for-spot-at-u23-africa-cup-of-49e741/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>The Diables Rouges must beat the Guinean Olympic selection in a two-legged tie starting at home on March 22.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:20:29 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" length="37606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Congo employers urge tax changes in 2027 budget review</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-employers-urge-tax-changes-in-2027-budget-review-6ce7b8/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-employers-urge-tax-changes-in-2027-budget-review-6ce7b8/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>UniCongo asked lawmakers to tax company income rather than turnover and revise rules on penalties, registration fees, VAT and payroll tax.</description><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:31:42 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-employers-urge-tax-changes-in-2027-budget-review-6ce7b8/share.jpg" length="41164" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-employers-urge-tax-changes-in-2027-budget-review-6ce7b8/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Congo hosts accord for diplomatic ties between Kenya and DR Congo</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-hosts-accord-for-diplomatic-ties-between-kenya-and-dr-fe85ea/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/cg/congo-hosts-accord-for-diplomatic-ties-between-kenya-and-dr-fe85ea/</guid><category>Republic of Congo</category><description>The two presidents agreed to pursue diplomatic channels, work toward the return of their ambassadors and expand regional cooperation.</description><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:51:21 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" length="37606" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/cg.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
